{# A LABELLED CONTROL IN THE PAGE-ACTION ROW — "Scope", "Compare with".

   THE CAPTION IS A LINE ABOVE THE BOX and never a placeholder inside it: a
   select whose first option names the question has no question left to show
   once somebody has answered it.

   IT IS A GET FORM PER CONTROL, submitted on change where there is a script
   and by the button beside it where there is none — the address is the
   state, so a scope somebody picked is a link they can send. Every other
   answer on the page travels as a hidden field, or picking a period would
   clear the scope.

   Variables:
     label   what the caption reads
     name    the query key this control owns
     chosen  the value it currently holds
     options value => label, in the order they read
     here    where the form submits
     carry   the other answers, as key => value
     small   the narrower box the design uses for the second and third #}
<label class="ov-ctl{{ small|default(false) ? ' sm' : '' }}">
    <span class="k">{{ label }}</span>
    <form method="get" action="{{ here }}">
        <span class="fsel">
            <select class="fld" name="{{ name }}" aria-label="{{ label }}" onchange="this.form.requestSubmit()">
                {% for value, option in options %}
                    <option value="{{ value }}"{{ value == chosen ? ' selected' : '' }}>{{ option }}</option>
                {% endfor %}
            </select>
        </span>
        {% for key, value in carry|default({}) %}<input type="hidden" name="{{ key }}" value="{{ value }}">{% endfor %}
        {# WITHOUT A SCRIPT THE ANSWER STILL TRAVELS. The button is the
           form's own submit, hidden from a pointer and reachable by a
           keyboard, so a page whose scripts never loaded is a page whose
           controls still work. #}
        <button class="visually-hidden" type="submit">Apply {{ label|lower }}</button>
    </form>
</label>
